From: hashtagbasit
Subject: Qualcomm: CPU and GPU temperature from thermal zones that read

The Lenovo tablets' 7.2.x kernels showed 0 C for both. The CPU zones there
are "cpuss0-thermal" / "cpu2-top-thermal" (no dash after cpuss, which the
earlier matching missed), a hwmon cpu sensor that reads 0 was kept, and the
GPU had no fallback when no hwmon named "gpu" exists. Match the zone types
on their prefix, drop a cpu sensor that reads 0, and read the hottest
gpuss thermal zone when the GPU hwmon is missing or reads 0.

---
--- a/src/cpu.cpp
+++ b/src/cpu.cpp
@@ -552,8 +552,10 @@
